    },
    {
      "section": "7.5",
      "label": "(2)",
      "text": "Before infusion, the door must be closed and locked. 150 (UC1.10 §4.1.1)",
      "id": null
    },
    {
      "section": "7.5",
      "label": "(3)",
      "text": "Hospital procedures must endow the attending clinician access to the door key 151, yet prevent other persons’ access. Key-handling processes are beyond the scope of these requirements, but much depends on the attending clinician: it’s the right drug, in the right patient, with the right prescription from a physician authorized to prescribe narcotics for those suﬀering great pain.",
      "id": null
